From 66da9d75380100af827ac023927cff64eabef1d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduard Moldovan <edimoldovan@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 02:44:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 09/24] arm64: dts: apple: Add T6050 and J714c

Add the Apple T6050 (M5 Max) SoC and the 14-inch MacBook Pro with it
(J714c), from the J714c Apple Device Tree:

- t6050-base.dtsi: 18 CPUs in two M clusters and one P cluster with
  their OPP tables, the timer and the reference clocks;
- t6050-die0.dtsi: AICv3, the serial port, the six PMGR blocks, the
  cluster cpufreq controllers, the watchdog, the keyboard backlight
  PWM, the GPIO block, I2C1-3, and the MTP with its mailbox, DART and
  DockChannel;
- t6050-pmgr.dtsi: 302 power domains. The four Type-C ports' CIO
  domains and atc3_common stay with the firmware: powering them at boot
  breaks the loader's USB 2.0 host setup;
- t6050-nvme.dtsi: the ANS2 NVMe controller with its mailbox and SART;
- t6050-smc.dtsi: the SMC with its GPIO, hwmon, RTC and (disabled)
  reboot children, and nub-spmi0 with the abbey PMIC NVMEM cells the RTC
  and reboot children read. Based on omarchy-m5's dt/t6050-smc.dtsi
  (github.com/betizzel/omarchy-m5, GPL-2.0+ OR MIT), with the full
  0x4000 nub-spmi0 window from rolotrealanis98's m5pro-linux.
  nub-spmi0 is polled: the gen 4 SPMI driver has no interrupt support.
  smc_reboot stays disabled: its restart handler would take over from
  the watchdog's, and its PMIC scratchpad offsets are not verified;
- t6050-j714c.dts: memory, the boot framebuffer marked as the built-in
  panel, the serial console, the keyboard and trackpad (trackpad
  firmware apple/tpmtfw-j714c.bin, power method 2 with firmware-managed
  reset: with power method 1 the MTP firmware answers the power-state
  request with "unknown power state"), the keyboard backlight
  (pwm-leds, 40000 ns period), and the SMC with the common, dual-fan
  and laptop sensors. The J714c SMC spells the fan mode keys F0md and
  F1md, so the board overrides apple,fan-mode.

The keyboard and trackpad need the loader to program the MTP DAPF
(m1n1 on T6050).

Tested on J714c, this series booted over the resident m1n1 into the
Omarchy root on the internal SSD: 18 CPUs with cpufreq on all three
clusters, the MTP keyboard and multi-touch devices, the SMC power/lid
input, kbd_backlight, AC and battery, the RTC, 13 hwmon inputs, and the
