From: TripleU613 <TripleU613@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:53:26 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 23/24] arm64: dts: apple: Add J714s (MacBook Pro 14-inch, M5
 Pro)

The 14-inch MacBook Pro with the M5 Pro (J714s, Mac17,9) is a T6050
board like the J716s. Add its device tree, in the shape of
t6050-j716s.dts: the MTP keyboard and trackpad, the keyboard backlight
on FPWM0, the SMC sensors with the T6050 fan mode keys, and the
loader-filled framebuffer and memory.

J714s values, all read from the J714s Apple Device Tree:
- trackpad: multi-touch PowerMethod 2; function-afe-reset is the SMC
  pcIO template 0x011c000000010000, the same value as on the J714c and
  J716s, so SMC pcIO output 28;
- keyboard backlight: pwm0 "fpwm,s5l8920x" at 0x505040000,
  kbd-backlight default-hz 25000 (period 40000 ns);
- CPUs: binned units list fewer cores in the ADT (the unit tested lists
  15 of 18: cpu5, cpu11 and cpu17 are absent). No core is disabled
  here; the loader removes the ones the ADT does not list, as for the
  other binned Apple SoCs.

The J714s firmware announces its accelerometer interface as "tp-accel"
rather than "tp_accel", so no node is added for it.

Tested on a J714s (Mac17,9, macOS 26.6.2 firmware) with our own 7.2.2
kernels, builds #28-#31 (AsahiLinux/linux 236788cd2 plus our patches),
whose T6050 nodes are at the same addresses as here but come from a
different base tree. There the SMC and keyboard-backlight nodes were
added at runtime by an overlay/changeset rather than a static DT. This
file itself has not been booted:
- the MTP keyboard and trackpad bind; with power method 2 the
  trackpad comes up ("Interface multi-touch is now ready") after the
  host pulses SMC pcIO output 28 (assert, then release);
- the SMC hwmon, power/lid input and RTC children probe with the same
  13 hwmon keys as hwmon-common/fan-dual/laptop with F0md/F1md;
- pwm-leds binds kbd_backlight on FPWM0 after genpd powers FPWM0
  (it is off at hand-off; build #28). Whether the light turns on was
  not seen.
Physical input, separately: on that earlier chain (our own loader and
7.2.2 kernels) the owner confirmed keyboard typing (builds FT9, FT14,
FT18-r2) and reported the trackpad working on the #30 boot. That does
not cover this DTS, which has not been booted.

Not covered: macsmc-power. On the same J714s an earlier kernel with
the macsmc-power work-init fix, but without "read battery identity
strings at their key size", hard-hung in the macsmc-power probe once.
It has not been retried.

Offline: cpp + dtc build of t6050-j714s.dtb with no warnings (the same
as t6050-j716s.dtb), dt-validate against the bindings.

Depends on the J716s series (#413) and the T6050 base (#404).

Prepared with AI assistance (Claude). The submitter must review the
change and add their Signed-off-by before it can be merged.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5 dtc dtschema
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/Makefile        |   1 +
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j714s.dts | 139 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 140 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j714s.dts

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/Makefile b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/Makefile
index 8b605c635d6cd4..1654e74706e5c8 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/Makefile
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/Makefile
@@ -95,6 +95,7 @@ dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_APPLE) += t6032-j575d.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_APPLE) += t6034-j514m.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_APPLE) += t6034-j516m.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_APPLE) += t6050-j714c.dtb
+dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_APPLE) += t6050-j714s.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_APPLE) += t6050-j716s.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_APPLE) += t8112-j413.dtb
 dtb-$(CONFIG_ARCH_APPLE) += t8112-j415.dtb
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j714s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j714s.dts
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000000..4c488bf6d34445
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j714s.dts
@@ -0,0 +1,139 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0+ OR MIT
+/*
+ * Apple MacBook Pro (14-inch, M5 Pro, 2026)
+ *
+ * target-type: J714s (Mac17,9)
+ *
+ * A T6050 laid out as on the J716s. Binned parts have fewer CPU cores
+ * (15 of 18 on the unit this was written on); the loader removes the
+ * cores the ADT does not list, as for the other binned Apple SoCs. The
+ * loader also supplies usable memory, CPU release addresses, framebuffer
+ * geometry and the keyboard layout. Peripheral power domains come from
+ * t6050-pmgr.dtsi; the framebuffer holds the display domain.
+ *
+ * Copyright The Asahi Linux Contributors
+ */
+
+/dts-v1/;
+
+#include <dt-bindings/gpio/gpio.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/apple-aic.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/interrupt-controller/irq.h>
+#include <dt-bindings/leds/common.h>
+
+#include "t6050.dtsi"
+#include "t6050-smc.dtsi"
+
+/ {
+	compatible = "apple,j714s", "apple,t6050", "apple,arm-platform";
+	#address-cells = <2>;
+	chassis-type = "laptop";
+	interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
+	model = "Apple MacBook Pro (14-inch, M5 Pro, 2026)";
+	#size-cells = <2>;
+
+	aliases {
+		keyboard = &keyboard;
+		serial0 = &serial0;
+	};
+
+	chosen {
+		ranges;
+		#address-cells = <2>;
+		#size-cells = <2>;
+		stdout-path = "serial0:1500000n8";
+
+		framebuffer@0 {
+			compatible = "apple,simple-framebuffer",
+				     "simple-framebuffer";
+			reg = <0 0 0 0>; /* Filled by the loader. */
+			power-domains = <&ps_disp_cpu>;
+			apple,internal-panel; /* simpledrm reports it as eDP */
+
+			/* m1n1 only enables it on chips it knows. */
+			status = "okay";
+		};
+	};
+
+	memory@10000000000 {
+		reg = <0x100 0 0 0>; /* Filled by the loader. */
+		device_type = "memory";
+	};
+
+	/* ADT pwm0/kbd-backlight: channel 0 at 25 kHz */
+	led-controller {
+		compatible = "pwm-leds";
+
+		led-0 {
+			color = <LED_COLOR_ID_WHITE>;
+			default-state = "keep";
+			function = LED_FUNCTION_KBD_BACKLIGHT;
+			label = "kbd_backlight";
+			max-brightness = <255>;
+			pwms = <&fpwm0 0 40000>;
+		};
+	};
+};
+
+&fpwm0 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&mtp {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&mtp_mbox {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&mtp_dart {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&mtp_dockchannel {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&mtp_hid {
+	/*
+	 * ADT multi-touch function-afe-reset = smc-pmu pKW8('pcIO', 0x10000,
+	 * 0x11c0000), SMC pcIO output 28 as on the J714c and J716s; level 1
+	 * asserts the reset.
+	 */
+	apple,afe-reset-gpios = <&smc_gpio 28 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+
+	actuator {
+	};
+
+	keyboard: keyboard {
+		hid-country-code = <0>;
+		apple,keyboard-layout-id = <0>;
+	};
+
+	multi-touch {
+		firmware-name = "apple/tpmtfw-j714s.bin";
+		apple,power-method = <2>;
+	};
+
+	stm {
+	};
+};
+
+#include "hwmon-common.dtsi"
+#include "hwmon-fan-dual.dtsi"
+#include "hwmon-laptop.dtsi"
+
+/*
+ * The T6050 SMC spells the fan mode keys F0md/F1md; F0Md/F1Md from
+ * hwmon-fan*.dtsi do not exist.
+ */
+&smc_hwmon {
+	fan-F0Ac {
+		apple,fan-mode = "F0md";
+	};
+
+	fan-F1Ac {
+		apple,fan-mode = "F1md";
+	};
+};

From 87d61271369d9f3f5974df8663f5d0f1f77031fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TripleU <182648541+TripleU613@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:12:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 24/24] gpio: macsmc: Drive the J714s trackpad AFE reset
 through pcIO

The J714s (MacBook Pro 14-inch, M5 Pro) Apple Device Tree describes the
multi-touch function-afe-reset with the same SMC pcIO template as the
J714c and J716s: pKW8('pcIO', 0x10000, 0x11c0000), output 28. Use the
shared table on the J714s too, so dockchannel-hid can get its
apple,afe-reset GPIO there; without it the J714s keyboard and trackpad
fail to probe with power method 2.

On a J714s, with our own 7.2.2 kernels (builds #29-#31, not this driver), two host writes
of that template, value 1 then value 0, made a multi-touch interface
that had timed out with firmware-managed reset come up ("Interface
multi-touch is now ready"). That was a one-shot from userspace through
our own SMC write path, not dockchannel-hid's OFF/ON sequence, which
has not run on a J714s. The active-high polarity is taken from the
J716s; on the J714s only the write order is consistent with it.
The owner separately reported the trackpad working on that earlier
chain (kernel build #30); that does not cover this driver path.

Validation note: a full-tree W=1 LLVM build of gpio-macsmc.o and of the
t6050-j714s/j716s DTBs on this branch passes with no warnings, and
CHECK_DTBS=y shows no new finding on j714s. The J714s DTS commit (the parent
of this one) was written before it; its native-test notes are clarified in
the PR description.

Prepared with AI assistance (Claude). The submitter must review the
change and add their Signed-off-by before it can be merged.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/gpio/gpio-macsmc.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpio/gpio-macsmc.c b/drivers/gpio/gpio-macsmc.c
index 60c776a7df44a2..61a724fb2dca26 100644
--- a/drivers/gpio/gpio-macsmc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpio/gpio-macsmc.c
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@ static const struct macsmc_pcio_line macsmc_j700_pcio[] = {
 	{ }
 };
 
-/* J714c and J716s: the same template in both Apple device trees */
+/* J714c, J714s and J716s: the same template in their Apple device trees */
 static const struct macsmc_pcio_line macsmc_j714c_pcio[] = {
 	/* multi-touch function-afe-reset: pKW8("pcIO", 0x10000, 0x11c0000) */
 	{ 28, 0x10000, 0x11c0000 },
@@ -324,6 +324,7 @@ static int macsmc_gpio_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		if (of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j700"))
 			smcgp->pcio = macsmc_j700_pcio;
 		else if (of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j714c") ||
+			 of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j714s") ||
 			 of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j716s"))
 			smcgp->pcio = macsmc_j714c_pcio;
 	}
